* Notrump openings

Booklet sections "GENERAL APPROACH", "RESPONSES AND LATER BIDDING AFTER A 15--17 1NT
OPENING", "INTERFERENCE AFTER A 1NT OPENING BID" and "RESPONSES TO A 2NT OR A 3NT
OPENING". A notrump opening may contain a 5-card suit, even a major. 2NT and 3NT
continue the same ladder (2NT = 20--21, 3NT = 25--27) and outrank 2!c for an
equivalent balanced hand, since SAYC treats the direct notrump bid as the more
specific call for those two ranges (see NOTES.md #2).

1N = {prio:90} 15--17 hcp, bal
2N = {prio:95} 20--21 hcp, bal
3N = {prio:101} 25--27 hcp, bal

** Responses to 1NT

Stayman is non-forcing (the auction may stop in 2 of a suit); opener bids 2H with
4-4 in the majors. Jacoby transfers are used for both majors; 2S is a minor-suit
relay showing both minors (a lower-frequency convention many partnerships do
not fully exploit, per the booklet's own annotation) -- opener must rebid 3C, and
responder passes with clubs or corrects to 3D with diamonds (see NOTES.md #13).

1N-
2C = !STAY NF, 8+ hcp, 4+!h or 4+!s
  2D = 0--3!s, 0--3!h
  2H = {prio:1} 4+!h
  2S = {prio:0} 4+!s, not 4+!h
2D = {prio:1} !TRF, 5+!h
  2H = {prio:0} unlimited
    P = 0--7 hcp
    2N = 8--9 hcp
    3C = F, 5+!c
    3D = F, 5+!d
    3S = F, 5+!s
    3N = CoG, 10--15 hcp, 5=!h
    4H = 10--15 hcp, 6+!h
  3H = {prio:1} MAX, 17 hcp, 4+!h
2H = {prio:1} !TRF, 5+!s
  2S = {prio:0} unlimited
    P = 0--7 hcp
    2N = 8--9 hcp
    3C = F, 5+!c
    3D = F, 5+!d
    3H = F, 5+!h
    3N = CoG, 10--15 hcp, 5=!s
    4S = 10--15 hcp, 6+!s
  3S = {prio:1} MAX, 17 hcp, 4+!s
2S = !TRF, 0--7 hcp, 6+!c or 6+!d
  3C = unlimited
    P = 6+!c
    3D = {prio:1} 6+!d
2N = 8--9 hcp, not 4+!h, not 4+!s
3C = INV, 6+!c
3D = INV, 6+!d
3H = {prio:2} S/T, 6+!h
3S = {prio:2} S/T, 6+!s
3N = 10--15 hcp, not 4+!h, not 4+!s
4C = !BW
4N = {prio:1} 16--17 hcp

*** Interference over 1NT

If an opponent doubles, Stayman and transfers stay on. If an opponent overcalls,
Stayman and transfers are off (bids are natural) except that a cuebid of the
overcaller's suit may substitute for Stayman with game-forcing strength. If the
opponents intervene over a conventional response, a further voluntary bid keeps its
normal meaning ("I have a real fit").

1N-(D)-
2C = !STAY NF, 8+ hcp
2D = !TRF, 5+!h
2H = !TRF, 5+!s

1N-(1X)-
2Y = NAT
2X = !cue, FG

** Responses to 2NT and 3NT

The same Stayman and Jacoby-transfer machinery is used one level higher for 2NT,
and two levels higher for 3NT.

2N-
3C = !STAY, 4+!h or 4+!s
3D = {prio:1} !TRF, 5+!h
3H = {prio:1} !TRF, 5+!s
4C = !BW
4N = {prio:1} 11--12 hcp

3N-
4C = !STAY, 4+!h or 4+!s
4D = {prio:1} !TRF, 5+!h
4H = {prio:1} !TRF, 5+!s
